## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS
- Man standing in the carriageway near the crossing — m0
- Man in white shirt standing among moving two-wheelers — m1
- Motorcyclist carrying a gas cylinder — m9
- Pedestrian in olive-green shirt crossing directly in front of moving traffic — m12
- Overloaded green-and-yellow CNG auto with red/blue tarpaulin load stationary for the whole clip — m19
- Woman in green outfit/dupatta appearing to interact with occupants near an auto — m29
- White Mercedes SUV in the moving lane during gridlock — m37
- Police vehicle with red-blue light bar — m49
- Man in grey shirt lingering among cars on the right — m47
- Yellow JCB-type construction vehicle at top right — m54
- White ambulance crossing top-left — m58

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
- Heavy mixed traffic continuously from m0 through m24, with gridlock clearing to free flow at m24.
- Severe congestion, lanes packed near-stationary, from m25 through m55 — the dominant condition of the footage.
- Flow toward the camera resumed from m56 onward.
- During the jam, multiple pedestrians moved between queued vehicles (m25, 29, 35, 36, 40, 41, 47, 49, 50, 56, 57, 58).

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
- Pedestrians walking/standing in the live carriageway among moving traffic — m0, m1.
- Pedestrian in olive-green shirt crossing directly in front of moving traffic — m12.
- Persistent lane-filtering by two-wheelers between queued/near-stationary lanes throughout the congestion (m25–59).
- No wrong-way driving, helmetless riders or red-light jumping were observed.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The hour divides into three phases. Minutes 0–24: continuous heavy but moving mixed traffic with a steady stream of identified vehicles, ending in gridlock that cleared at m24. Minutes 25–55: severe, near-stationary gridlock dominating the junction, with goods vehicles, buses (including the stationary Nirma University bus, m25–27) and tractors trapped in the queue, two-wheelers filtering through, and pedestrians routinely walking between vehicles. Minutes 56–59: flow resumed toward the camera, with a fresh set of vehicles passing, including a police van at m59. Dominant traffic throughout was private cars (white most common) with green-and-yellow autos and helmeted two-wheeler riders ever-present. Recurring elements: goods three-wheelers with tarpaulin loads, red tractors/tankers, red city buses, pedestrians in green clothing, and damp road surfaces indicating recent rain.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. The junction carried heavy traffic for the entire 60 minutes; even the "free flow" phases (m24, m56–59) were busy.
