## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
- Red-light jumping: a white car, a dark car and several autos jumped a red signal showing amber/red (538); an ambulance with beacon apparently ran a red light (654).
- Helmetless riders observed repeatedly, particularly from minute 171 onward (e.g. 171–174, 273, 316, 373, 388, 575–599, 625–649, 673); "little evident signal discipline" noted generally around minutes 225–249.
- No wrong-way driving observed. Stationary/parked vehicles noted at minutes 85, 193–196, 383, 514, 535, 588, 670, 703, 705, 718–719 (no enforcement action implied).

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The footage covers a full overnight cycle at a busy signalised junction. From 20:59 to roughly midnight (mins 0–175) traffic was busy but steady, dominated by cars, auto-rickshaws and buses, with the same white hatchback recurring almost every minute — a pattern the observations themselves flag as a possible repeating loop vehicle. From midnight to ~05:00 (mins 175–549) traffic thinned progressively to light, free-flowing overnight levels dominated by two-wheelers and yellow-green auto-rickshaws, with goods vehicles, coaches and occasional emergency/police vehicles passing through; pedestrian crowds on the right footpath peaked in this window (20–50 people) even as crossings became rare. From ~05:19 (mins 500–719) traffic built again into light-to-moderate morning flow dominated by yellow-and-green CNG auto-rickshaws (4–15 per minute), motorcycles/scooters (8–20 per minute, many with pillions and many helmetless), white cars, and frequent red and blue-and-white city buses including double-deckers and branded coaches. Wet/reflective road surfaces recurred throughout, indicating intermittent rain across both nights. Signal phases cycled red/amber/green throughout, with the camera-facing approach frequently showing amber/red. The "DELIGHT P1 RLVD" red-light-enforcement overlay was a persistent on-screen feature from ~minute 124 onward. No makes, models or plates were legible for the vast majority of the footage due to darkness, distance and motion blur.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
- Minutes 300–549: consistently light, free-flowing overnight traffic with no incidents, queues or unusual behaviour (notably mins 300–499, described as "very light" pre-dawn flow).
- Minutes 550–719: light, free-flowing early-morning traffic with no incidents; pedestrian activity minimal.
- Minutes 269, 273–274: no pedestrians at all.
- Minutes 185, 197, 198: no data (clips unprocessed).
- No alerts, collisions (other than the single apparent collision at minute 599), stopped traffic or suspicious activity were recorded at any point in the 720-minute period.
