==============================================================================
# POLICE SUMMARY — CCTV REVIEW
**Camera:** cam15_stream-15 ("Suvidhapark P3 RLVD"), Suvidhapark junction
**Footage:** 720 minutes (minutes 1–719), night of 13-06-2026 ~21:00 through morning of 14-06-2026 ~08:59

---

## 1. SCENE
The camera overlooks a signalised road junction (RLVD-equipped) at Suvidhapark, with zebra crossings, footpaths, a far-side crossing and a left slip road. Footage begins on Saturday night 13-06-2026 (21:00) and runs through Sunday 14-06-2026 to ~08:59. Lighting was night-time headlight/streetlight glare for roughly the first 210 minutes, switching to greyscale infrared/monochrome around minute 211, remaining IR through the pre-dawn hours, and returning to colour/daylight from roughly minute 521 onward. Image quality was consistently poor: heavy glare, motion blur, compression/pixelation and corrupted frames throughout (e.g. minutes 25, 32, 36, 47, 51, 60, 62, 500, 501, 550, 552, 573, 582, 591, 592, 599, 682, 685, 692, 711, 714). The road surface appeared wet/reflective in many minutes (e.g. 31, 34, 46, 77–78, 84–85, 152, 158, 160, 165, 174, 277, 283, 286, 296, 298, 302, 304, 308, 316, 319–324, 401, 408, 423), suggesting recent or ongoing rain.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE
Traffic was dominated throughout by two-wheelers — motorcycles/scooters at roughly 8–25 per minute at peak (evening), 6–20 per minute overnight and morning, frequently carrying pillion riders (occasionally two pillions or three occupants total, e.g. minutes 58, 106, 155–156, 714), many apparently helmetless. Green-and-yellow auto-rickshaws recurred in nearly every period, becoming the dominant visible type in the early morning (minutes 525–549, 575–599). Cars were mostly white, silver/grey, dark/black, with occasional red, maroon, blue, gold/beige and brown examples (e.g. dark blue sedan min 1; red compact SUV min 6; maroon car min 10; red/dark hatchback min 85; maroon SUV min 92; red SUV mins 108, 563; blue hatchback min 179; black MPV min 563; silver sedan min 560; brown/maroon SUV min 566). Buses were a constant feature: numerous liveries including "PATEL" coach (mins 54–55), "WWW.FTTBUS.IN"/"Daney" white coach (min 69), "Deep Travels" coach with Khanda emblem (min 77), "TANWA"/"TANNA" buses (mins 89–90), red-liveried bus with Gujarati LED destination (min 95), "Tirth" bus (min 105), GSRTC-style bus (min 111), "RAMANI" bus (min 113), "JALARAM" tour coach (min 158), red city buses (mins 529, 627, 635, 644, 649 — one route "38/4"), blue city buses (mins 530, 549, 626, 631, 685, 687, 712, 718), "UNITY" bus with horse artwork (min 682), "BHARAT BENZ" bus (min 666), "NEDARABAD" bus (min 561), "RAJ"/"TESLA" bus (min 572), pink-and-blue city bus (min 707). Goods vehicles included a white-and-yellow truck and blue goods truck (min 56), cement mixer and yellow truck (min 95), white box/container truck (min 90), tractor with two trailers (min 218), tractors (mins 234, 634, 667, 678, 690, 694), yellow DHL box truck (min 656), white "BHARAT BENZ" bus (min 666), white TATA tipper (mins 521–522), blue tipper (min 523), refuse trucks (mins 556, 600, 606), red container truck (min 559), tanker truck (min 707), multi-axle lorries (mins 284, 417, 423, 498). Ambulance-type vans appeared at minutes 172, 183, 594, 632, 667 and 700; a white car with blue and red emergency lights was stationary at the far-left corner for the whole of minute 18. Non-motorised traffic included cyclists (mins 3, 24, 25, 26, 29, 30, 32, 35, 40, 54, 70, 274, 651, 662, 671), cycle rickshaws/handcarts (mins 531, 564, 606, 620, 668, 680, 683, 688, 697) and a road-sweeping machine (min 684). Animals: stray dogs at minutes 197, 305, 348, 349, 408, 409, 525, 539, 566, 568 (three dogs), 582, 591, 592, 597, 613; cows at minutes 357, 386, 429.

People: pedestrians were frequent in the evening and morning and almost absent overnight. Notable individuals include a person in a white shirt (min 2), two crossing right-to-left (min 5), a person in a yellow shirt and white pants (min 14), a man in a light shirt crossing the carriageway (mins 31, 33), a woman in pale pink (min 32), three women in white, light-blue and red/maroon (min 42), a man in white kurta-pyjama (min 542), a woman in a long pink/fuchsia outfit (min 534), a street sweeper in hi-vis (min 655), a traffic warden in hi-vis (min 651), a woman in a red/pink patterned sari (mins 672–675), a woman in an orange/mustard saree (min 699), a woman in a red/maroon sari (min 703), a group of six to eight people dressed in white (min 552), an elderly man in all-white making a long slow crossing (min 571), a barefoot man in white vest and blue shorts (min 199), a pedestrian walking a pale dog on the zebra (min 523), and a man in a red shirt with a dog (min 523). A small group of 3–5 people stood near the emergency-light vehicle at minute 18.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

**CONFIRMED:**
