# CCTV ANALYSIS SUMMARY — cam17_17_Rajkot_Bus_Port_CCTV
**Location:** Rajkot Bus Port | **Footage:** 718 minutes (cam17_17_Rajkot_Bus_Port_CCTV.mp4), fixed camera
**Dates observed in timestamps:** 13-06-2026 and 14-06-2026 (with multiple discontinuities)

---

## 1. SCENE

The camera is fixed on a covered pavement forecourt, two-wheeler parking bay and public road at Rajkot Bus Port. Persistent landmarks throughout: closed shop shutters, signage reading "HOTEL JK", a "COTTON" advertisement (ph. 87339 29701/702) and a "BUS EXIT ONLY" sign; a raised planter/median with bollards and a low kerb/ledge. The footage spans daylight, pre-dawn darkness and night. Lighting jumps anomalously within single minutes (minute 80 daylight-to-dark; minute 200 daylight-to-night mid-clip). From roughly minute 81 onward the scene is pre-dawn/night, remaining dark through approximately minute 365, then returning to daylight/early-morning brightness (minutes 366–~424 show night from ~01:02, then day/morning around minutes 445+), with further night-time segments to the end of the footage (21:05, 13-06-2026). The road surface appears wet/reflective in many segments (minutes 46–47, 88, 94–95, 225–249, 351–374, 375–399, 400–424, 450–499, 550–699), suggesting recent rain. All shop shutters remained closed for the whole 718 minutes.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

**Traffic:** Steady flow of green-and-yellow (and some black-and-yellow) auto-rickshaws in nearly every segment — 6–10 at a time at peaks (minutes 51, 61–62, 71, 145, 163). Numerous buses throughout, predominantly GSRTC-liveried (blue-and-white, orange/white, red/cream, white "Premium Services", dark, light-blue, sleeper coaches) plus red-and-white, red/pink, white city buses, a white/teal GSRTC coach, a white/silver bus, a white-and-green coach, a large white luxury coach (minute 605), a light blue coach with "ESSE…" lettering (minute 128) and a red/maroon city bus with cream banding (minute 40). Cars/vans: white cars and vans most frequent, plus dark, silver, hatchbacks, white SUVs, a grey/dark MPV, a dark SUV (minutes 551, 706, 716), a red truck (minute 61), a red goods truck (minute 61), a white truck/coach, a dark-cab truck (minute 599), a white light commercial van (minute 559) and a tractor with trailer (minute 181). Motorcycles and scooters with riders, a cyclist (minutes 42, 61), a bicycle (minute 45), a cyclist in a light shirt (~minute 580), a small white three-wheeler/e-rickshaw-style vehicle (minute 71) and a white/grey goods three-wheeler parked at the left edge (minutes 508, 512, 516, 523). An ambulance with flashing red lights passed at minute 610 (0–5s) — the only emergency vehicle. A blue three-wheeler goods carrier with blue-and-white water drums/gas cylinders was parked at the left kerb being loaded/unloaded by a worker through minutes 19–22.

**Parked vehicles:** A consistently static bay of roughly 4–15 two-wheelers (mostly black motorcycles/scooters, plus white, grey/silver, maroon/dark scooters, a dark scooter with red wheel stripes/rims, a black cruiser-style motorcycle with brown seat recurring across the whole footage, a motorcycle with blue tank detailing, one with "Access"-style text, and various branded machines noted in Section 3). A white hatchback parked at the left kerb recurs across long night segments (minutes 75–99, 200–324, 325–349, 350–374, 406–409, 444–499), with doors/boot open at times. A white MPV/car with rear door open (minute 275); a white MPV entered and parked at minute 384. A green-and-yellow auto-rickshaw parked at the left edge (minutes 490+, 644+, 650–674, 680–690, 705–708).

**People:** Total pedestrian counts ranged from near-zero in pre-dawn hours to 10–25 per frame at peak (minute 163; 15–20 in minute 196; 10–20 in minute 576). Recurring categories:
- **Pavement sleepers:** groups of roughly 3–10 people sleeping on the raised pavement against the closed shutter, from minute 81 onward intermittently (minutes 81–99, 100–104, 200–249, 250–274, 275–299 — growing from 2–3 to 6–10; 300–365), re-forming again (minutes 390–399, 400–424, 445–449, 450–499, 500–524, 669–673). Notable sleepers included one in a white/light shirt with dark trousers and white sneakers beside them, one in dark polka-dot clothing, one in red/checkered clothing, one under a red-patterned blanket.
